    "template": "QMH Cancer Reporting Template - GI-Esophagus (Oesophageal carcinoma)",
    "url": "https://awiloqmh.github.io/CancerReportingTemplate/GI-Esophagus.html",
    "staging": "AJCC 8th edition pTNM, oesophagus chapter: separate pathological stage-group tables for squamous cell carcinoma and adenocarcinoma (grade and, for pT3 N0 squamous cases, the tumour zone decide the group), plus one shared ypTNM table after neoadjuvant therapy. pT derives from the tumour extension pick-list (adjacent-structure detail separates T4a from T4b), pN from the involved-node count (1-2 / 3-6 / 7+), pM1 from the distant-metastasis checks. Neuroendocrine and undifferentiated carcinomas follow the squamous table as G3; NETs are not AJCC-staged.",
    "stagingProtocol": "oesophagus",
    "grading": "WHO 2019 (digestive tumours): G1 well, G2 moderate, G3 poor / undifferentiated, GX cannot be assessed; neuroendocrine neoplasms carry their own grade and are not G-graded here."
  },
